    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16862": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student Conduct/ Community Standards",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Director, Student Conduct/ Community Standards Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Director, Student Conduct/ Community Standards Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02178 Job Title Assistant Director, Student Conduct/ Community Standards Position Number 107615 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level : 11 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range:  $75,000 - $81,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department VP Student Affrs. Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by September14, 2026. Applications received after September 14, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Ensure that student behavior aligns with and supports the University’s mission by investigating and adjudicating community standards violations both on and off campus. Provide proactive education and outreach to the campus community on topics related to community standards. Be responsible for comprehensive case management, data analysis, and the development of educational initiatives aimed at promoting a respectful and safe community environment. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Investigate, adjudicate and maintain accurate records regarding alleged violations of community standards by students and student organizations that include but are not limited to allegations of sexual misconduct, hazing and bullying. Assist in the facilitation and administration of the student conduct process and serve as a resource on community standard matters for students, faculty and staff. Assist with the development of community standards, revisions of policies and procedures, and handbook revisions. Ensure consistency and fairness for all student discipline. Serve as an administrative hearing officer and prepare cases for hearing panels. As needed, assist with the adjudication of Off-campus community standards violations. Collaborate extensively with conduct administrators, Housing and Residential Life staff, Campus Police, faculty and staff regarding student conduct issues. Collect and analyze data regarding student conduct and the conduct system. Develop presentations, statistical reports and summaries as needed. Assist with the ongoing training to ensure that the department is in compliance with Clery regulations and Stop Campus Hazing Act reporting requirements. Manage the data collection and reporting of Clery crimes for the Annual Safety Report in collaboration with URI PD. Assist with the selection, training, and implementation of hearing boards which include faculty, staff and students. Advise hearing panels. Assist with the selection, training, and implementation of conduct advisors, which include faculty, staff and students. Serve as a member of the student conduct team. Participate in the creation and implementation of educational programs and training to prevent violations of community standards. Assist in the development of student conduct/community standards and publication materials, website updates, and training manuals. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Represent the Dean of Students Office on University, Division and other committees and at University events. Work evenings and weekends as necessary. Perform additional duties as necessary. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers and printers; word processing, database management and spreadsheet software. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : Master’s degree in college student personnel or higher education, or related field. Minimum three years of professional experience in a college setting. Demonstrated evidence of attention to detail and collaborative work style. Demonstrated experience with evaluation, assessment. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Demonstrated ability to support student education and/or student growth. Demonstrated ability to interpret institutional policies, plans, objectives, rules and regulations, and to communicate the interpretation to others. Demonstrated ability to prepare and present detailed studies and reports and to make recommendations concerning the substance of the studies and reports. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Demonstrated ability to utilize Maxient software, including analytics. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : Demonstrated experience with evaluation, assessment, mediation, conflict resolution and/or campus judicial systems. Demonstrated knowledge of Title IX, Campus Save Act and Clery Act as they relate to sexual assault investigations on college campuses. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 07/20/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16846 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master’s degree in college student personnel or higher education, or related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum three years of professional experience in a college setting? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated evidence of attention to detail and collaborative work style? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with evaluation, assessment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to support student education and/or student growth? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to interpret institutional policies, plans, objectives, rules and regulations, and to communicate the interpretation to others? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to prepare and present detailed studies and reports and to make recommendations concerning the substance of the studies and reports? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to utilize Maxient software, including analytics? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
