    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16889": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Professor, Nursing",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Clinical Professor, Nursing Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Clinical Professor, Nursing Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Clinical Professor, Nursing Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ______________________________________________________________________________________________________ The College of Nursing is searching for a faculty member for a clinical track position to begin in Fall 2026. Experience in clinical nursing practice is required. POSTING SUMMARY : The College of Nursing ( CON ) is committed to excellence in teaching, scientific inquiry, and knowledge development. We are seeking a faculty member who will embrace our new college tagline, “Nurse leaders transforming wellbeing and environments,” and who has a strong record of clinical expertise that supports our mission. Our mission is to prepare nurses to excel as outstanding and compassionate clinicians, scholars, and leaders who will enhance the health and healthcare of individuals, families, communities, and populations both locally and globally. The successful candidate will have an appointment with the College of Nursing with primary responsibilities in clinical teaching, with possible classroom teaching, at the undergraduate and graduate levels as appropriate. The candidate will be expected to conduct teaching in clinical, collaborate for placements for students, and collaborate regarding faculty/preceptors as appropriate, participate in student advising and service to the college, and contribute to scholarly activities. KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Contribute as appropriate to the university’s undergraduate and graduate teaching missions by teaching clinical and other courses as assigned, while mentoring students for the college. Contribute to scholarship. Service as an advisor, mentor, and professional role model to students. Service to the college, university, and professional organizations. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as assigned. ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Ph.D. or DNP degree at the time of appointment. 2. Proficiency in written communication skills. 3. Proficiency in oral communication skills. 4. Strong interpersonal skills. 5. Clinical expertise in nursing. 6. Eligible for RN and/or APRN licensure in Rhode Island. 7. Ability to work with diverse groups/populations. PREFERRED : Clinical practice experience in pediatrics, but open to other areas of clinical expertise. Demonstrated experience in clinical and classroom teaching. Evidence and potential for clinical scholarship. ______________________________________________________________________________________________________ URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union AAUP - American Assoc of Univ Professors Status Academic Year, Full-time, Non-tenure-track, Limited End Date of Restriction or Limitation The position is full-time, academic year, non-tenure, limited to 09/25/2026 with anticipated renewal. Department Information Department Dean Nursing Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Information Position Number 107785 Posting Number F00499 Posting Date 11/07/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/15907 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have or will have a Ph.D. or DNP degree at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do you have clinical expertise in nursing? Yes No * Are you eligible for RN and/or APRN licensure in Rhode Island? Yes No * Do you have ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16514": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor, PhD Program Director",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Associate/Full Professor, PhD Program Director - Human Development &amp; Family Science Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Associate/Full Professor, PhD Program Director - Human Development & Family Science Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 5 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Research Plan - description of current research activity and future research directions. (#4) Other Document - teaching & diversity statement. (#5) Other Document - PDF reprints of up to 3 publications that you feel best highlight your suitability for the position (not necessarily those publications in journals with the highest impact factor) (as one complete pdf document). Please Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Associate/Full Professor, PhD Program Director - Human Development & Family Science Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by April 4, 2026. Applications received after April 4, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Position Summary: The Department of Human Development & Family Science at the University of Rhode Island invites applications for a tenure-track Associate or Full Professor who will also serve as the Program Director for the PhD in Health Sciences, an interdisciplinary program in the College of Health Sciences. We are looking for a leader with extensive experience obtaining external funding for research and mentoring graduate students and who complements the mission of the Department, College, and University. We have a particular emphasis on applied research aimed at improving the quality of life for individuals, families, and communities. Appointment will be made at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, depending on qualifications. The position is a 9-month appointment. We seek an accomplished scholar whose research and teaching address early stages of development across the lifespan and child health. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: child health and well-being, connections between physical and mental health, child life and pediatric health services, lifespan development, and medical social work. The Human Development & Family Science Department is located within the College of Health Sciences and is recognized for excellence in teaching, research, service, and experiential education. The Department includes high quality outreach programs, including child development centers and couple and family therapy clinics. The Department’s faculty lead several research laboratories/programs, conducting research in individual and family wellness across the lifespan. The PhD in Health Sciences is an interdisciplinary program with specializations in physical therapy, kinesiology, nutrition, communicative disorders, and human development & family science. The Department, College, and University recognize the importance of contributions from a broad range of perspectives. The Department of Human Development & Family Science is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion and seeks to serve as a representative inspiration for the next generations. As such, we particularly welcome candidates from groups historically underrepresented, marginalized, and/or excluded in the field of human development & family science who will support the mission of both URI and the College of Health Sciences to expose students to different perspectives. Candidates will demonstrate a commitment to inclusivity to enhance a sense of belonging and academic success among students from diverse cultures and backgrounds. Qualifications Required: 1. A PhD or equivalent terminal academic degree in human development & family science, social work, or a closely related field. 2. Record of teaching, research, and service commensurate with a tenured faculty appointment at the rank of associate or full professor. 3. Experience in teaching and mentoring graduate students, including PhD students. 4. Track record of successfully securing external research funding and having a strong scholarship record. 5. Strong leadership, teamwork, organizational, and communication skills. 6. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred: 1. Clinical background with licensure (e.g., social work or related professional license). 2. Leadership experience in graduate education. 3. Experience in human development and family science programs. 4. Demonstrated experience in interdepartmental and interdisciplinary collaboration. 5. Demonstrated successful teaching in areas of family and community health and early lifespan development. 6. Experience working within medical or healthcare systems. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union AAUP - American Assoc of Univ Professors Status Academic Year, Full-time, Tenure-track, Permanent End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Human Development & Family Science Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 5 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Research Plan – description of current research activity and future research directions. (#4) Other Document – teaching & diversity statement. (#5) Other Document – PDF reprints of up to 3 publications that you feel best highlight your suitability for the position (not necessarily those publications in journals with the highest impact factor) (as one complete pdf document). Please Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Information Position Number 109542 Posting Number F00514 Posting Date 03/10/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16146 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Research Plan Other Document Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD or equivalent terminal academic degree in human development & family science, social work, or a closely related field? Yes No * Do you have record of teaching, research, and service commensurate with a tenured faculty appointment at the rank of associate or full professor? Yes No * Do you have experience in teaching and mentoring graduate students, including PhD students? Yes No * Do you have track record of successfully securing external research funding and having a strong scholarship record? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
