    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16793": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant I",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Executive Assistant I Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Executive Assistant I Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02166 Job Title Executive Assistant I Position Number 108459 FTE 1.00 FLSA Non-Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 7 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range:  $60,000 - $68,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Dean Arts & Sciences Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by July 18, 2026. Applications received after July 18, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSTING SUMMARY : Report directly to the Dean of the College of Arts & Sciences, providing critical administrative support and performing private administrative duties of a complex, confidential and responsible nature. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Assist the Dean in carrying out administrative responsibilities; research and troubleshoot issues needing resolution at the College level. Provide confidential administrative services, including the following: arrange and schedule meetings; type reports, correspondence, speeches, financial forms, and related materials; make travel arrangements; draft and respond to routine correspondence; proofread sabbatical, annual review, promotion and tenure materials; prepare agendas and take and transcribe minutes; prepare and maintain spreadsheets; establish and maintain e-mail lists for College councils; in consultation with the Dean, develop and maintain College files, and ensure their confidentiality. Arrange, schedule, support, and conduct special events, such as meetings, conferences, and fundraising events. Support marketing and outreach efforts as necessary. Arrange alumni campus visits and alumni career workshops in coordination with A&S Director of Development and Career Services. Answer phones, respond to e-mail, greet visitors to the Dean’s Office area, and disseminate information to a diverse constituency. Deal directly with the public, students, faculty, staff, and officials (both within and outside the University community) on behalf of the Dean. Prioritize responses to correspondence, phone calls, and various issues, to manage demands on the Dean’s time. Interview and recommend for appointment administrative and student help within the Office. Train, schedule and assign workloads to student help and support staff. Project management for one-off initiatives pertaining to the Dean’s Office. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers; word processing, spreadsheet, and presentation & scheduling software; e-mail; social media; e-Campus software, Brightspace; fax and copying machines; calculator. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. High school diploma or GED . 2. Minimum of three years of responsible experience in an administrative support position (may include administrative work in a graduate assistantship) in a professional environment. 3. Demonstrated time management and organizational skills in a multiple-priority environment. 4. Demonstrated attention to detail. 5. Demonstrated computer skills (i.e. word processing, spreadsheets, presentation & scheduling software). 6. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 7. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 8. Demonstrated supervisory experience. 9. Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality. 10. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree. 2. Demonstrated experience in higher education administration. 3. Demonstrated knowledge of URI Policies, Processes, and systems. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 06/24/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16785 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a High school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of three years of responsible experience in an administrative support position (may include administrative work in a graduate assistantship) in a professional environment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated time management and organizational skills in a multiple-priority environment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated attention to detail? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated computer skills (i.e. word processing, spreadsheets, presentation & scheduling software)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated supervisory experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
