    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16895": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Professor of Pharmacy Practice",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Clinical Professor of Pharmacy Practice Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Clinical Professor of Pharmacy Practice Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Clinical Professor of Pharmacy Practice Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by August 12, 2026. Applications received after August 12, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ The University of Rhode Island College of Pharmacy invites applications for a full-time, academic-year (9-month), non-tenure-track Clinical Assistant Professor position in the Department of Pharmacy Practice and Clinical Research. The position will contribute to the College’s teaching, clinical practice, service, and scholarly missions, with primary teaching responsibilities in the Pharmacy Practice and Care Process ( PPCP )/Integrated Pharmacy Laboratory ( IPL ) sequence, Capstone courses, and other clinical courses within the Doctor of Pharmacy curriculum as needed. The successful candidate will establish and maintain a clinical practice site in a clinic or ambulatory care setting that supports the expansion of pharmacist-provided patient care services, particularly for rural, underserved, and marginalized populations. The faculty member will also engage in service to the Department, College, University, profession, and community and pursue scholarly activities related to clinical practice, pharmacy education, community engagement, health disparities, or other areas aligned with the faculty member’s expertise and interests. The anticipated start date is September 1, 2026. This is a full-time, academic year, non-tenure-track, limited, renewable appointment, with continuation contingent upon successful performance review and programmatic needs. KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Teaching and Mentorship Deliver instruction and facilitate active learning in the Pharmacy Practice and Care Process ( PPCP )/Integrated Pharmacy Laboratory ( IPL ) sequence (I–V). Lead and support skills-based education, including patient counseling and communication, prescription processing and clinical decision-making, drug information and medication therapy management, sterile and non-sterile compounding, physical assessment, and point-of-care skills. Contribute to Capstone courses through case-based instruction, simulation activities, student assessment, course coordination, and activities designed to prepare students for Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experiences (APPEs) and contemporary pharmacy practice. Deliver instruction in other required and elective clinical courses within the Doctor of Pharmacy curriculum based on departmental and programmatic needs and the faculty member’s areas of expertise. Facilitate recitations, simulations, case-based learning activities, and interprofessional education experiences. Assess student performance through skills-based assessments, Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs), written assignments, care plans, and other appropriate assessment methods. Provide timely feedback, remediation, coaching, and mentorship to support student development and professional growth. Contribute to course and curricular assessment, continuous quality improvement, and curriculum development. Oversee and mentor Teaching Assistants, pharmacy residents, and other learners assigned to relevant courses and educational activities. Precept Doctor of Pharmacy students completing experiential education rotations. Clinical Practice and Professional Service Establish and maintain a high-quality clinical practice site in collaboration with a partnering clinic or healthcare organization. Develop, implement, and evaluate pharmacist-provided patient care services designed to improve medication use, health outcomes, and access to care. Provide direct patient care services within the scope of pharmacist practice and applicable state laws and regulations. Collaborate with physicians, pharmacists, nurses, social workers, community health workers, and other healthcare professionals to provide patient-centered, team-based care. Support initiatives designed to expand access to pharmacist-provided services for rural, underserved, marginalized, and other populations experiencing barriers to healthcare. Develop a clinical practice environment that provides opportunities for student pharmacists, pharmacy residents, and other health professions learners. Contribute professional expertise to community organizations, healthcare partners, professional associations, and other external stakeholders as appropriate. Scholarship Develop and maintain a program of scholarly activity consistent with the expectations of a non-tenure-track Clinical Assistant Professor. Pursue internal and external funding opportunities to support clinical practice innovation, pharmacy education, community-engaged initiatives, healthcare access, health equity, or other areas aligned with the faculty member’s expertise and interests. Disseminate scholarly work through peer-reviewed publications, professional presentations, reports, educational scholarship, or other appropriate scholarly products. Collaborate with faculty, students, healthcare professionals, and community partners on scholarly and grant-funded initiatives. College, University, and Professional Service Participate in departmental, College, and University governance and service activities, including appointment to standing and ad hoc committees. Contribute to curriculum development, assessment, accreditation activities, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. Participate in faculty meetings, strategic planning activities, student recruitment, and other activities supporting the missions of the Department and College. Engage in service to professional organizations, healthcare organizations, community partners, or other external organizations as appropriate. Collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and external partners to advance the teaching, practice, service, and scholarly missions of the College. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as assigned. ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) degree from an ACPE -accredited college or university. 2. Completion of a PGY1 pharmacy residency. 3. Minimum of three years of pharmacy practice experience. 4. Licensed or eligible for pharmacist licensure in Rhode Island. 5. Experience providing direct patient care and applying the Pharmacists’ Patient Care Process. 6. Experience precepting student pharmacists or other health professions learners. 7. Demonstrated strong interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. 8. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, healthcare professionals, community partners, and interprofessional teams. 9. Demonstrated effective teaching, presentation, and facilitation skills. 10. Demonstrated commitment to working effectively with diverse populations and fostering inclusive learning and clinical practice environments. PREFERRED : 1. Prior didactic, laboratory, or experiential teaching experience in a Doctor of Pharmacy or other health professions program. 2. Experience providing care to rural, underserved, marginalized, or other populations experiencing barriers to healthcare. 3. Experience providing pharmacist services under a Collaborative Practice Agreement ( CPA ) or other collaborative patient care model. 4. Experience coordinating courses, laboratory sequences, simulations, or large-scale student assessments. 5. Evidence of scholarly productivity or demonstrated potential for scholarly contributions. 6. Experience developing, implementing, expanding, or evaluating pharmacist-provided patient care services. 7. APhA Pharmacy-Based Immunization Delivery certification or willingness to obtain certification. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union Non-Tenure Track Status Academic Year, Full-time, Non-tenure-track, Limited End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Dean Pharmacy Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Information Position Number 108636 Posting Number F00525 Posting Date 07/29/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16893 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) degree from an ACPE-accredited college or university? Yes No * Do you have completion of a PGY1 pharmacy residency? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of three years of pharmacy practice experience? Yes No * Are you licensed or eligible for pharmacist licensure in Rhode Island? Yes No * Do you have experience providing direct patient care and applying the Pharmacists’ Patient Care Process? Yes No * Do you have experience precepting student pharmacists or other health professions learners? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, healthcare professionals, community partners, and interprofessional teams? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated effective teaching, presentation, and facilitation skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated commitment to working effectively with diverse populations and fostering inclusive learning and clinical practice environments? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16521": {
      "title": "The search will remain open until the position has been filled.",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Part-time Faculty, User Experience Graduate Certificate Program Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Part-time Faculty, User Experience Graduate Certificate Program Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) CV with contact information for three (3) professional references (outside URI), as one complete document. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Part-time Faculty, User Experience Graduate Certificate Program Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ Qualified candidates who are not selected for employment for fall semester 2024 will have their applications remain active for two (2) years should a future opportunity arise during the 2025–2026 instructional year, September 1, 2025–August 31, 2026. The Department of Professional and Public Writing in the Harrington School of Communication and Media and College of Arts and Sciences seeks part-time faculty to teach online graduate courses for the UX Graduate Certificate Program on a per-course basis. Areas of instruction include ethical foundations of UX design, UX research and methods, UX and microcopy writing, and interaction design. As the largest college at the University of Rhode Island, the College of Arts and Sciences brings together and supports undergraduate programs across the arts, humanities, sciences, and social sciences. The college is committed to excellence in teaching and its academic units create learning experiences that stress the free and rigorous pursuit of knowledge, intellectual curiosity, respect for differences across cultures and perspectives, a passion for personal expression, and an investment in the responsibilities of an educated global citizen in a democratic society. The College facilitates students’ development into leaders and global citizens who think critically and creatively, communicate effectively, and participate actively in local and global communities. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : A selected candidate will teach one (1) or two (2) courses in the Department of Professional and Public Writing. Courses are asynchronous and delivered in an accelerated 7-week format. Part-time faculty are not required to engage in research or service activities but must hold regular office hours and be available to assist students enrolled in their courses. They are expected to stay current in their fields of instruction and with pedagogical methods and instructional technologies. Online teaching requires certification and possibly training by the University. Courses are three (3) credits. Specific responsibilities include: Delivering online lessons and assignments in UX Design principles, tools, and techniques through our course management platform (Brightspace) Providing regular feedback, guidance, and mentoring support to students to facilitate their learning and skill development while conveying confidence in every student’s ability to learn Cultivating a collaborative and participatory online learning environment that values diversity of people, ideas, cultures, and forms of expression Evaluating student performance and progress and providing timely assessment Fostering a safe environment that respects the diversity of people and ideas by modeling respect for all students and conveying confidence in every student’s ability to learn Qualifications: Required: 1. Master’s degree in technical communication or related field or a bachelor’s degree and three (3) years of professional experience in areas such as UX research, UX analytics, UX writing and/or content design, usability and heuristic evaluation, accessibility, wireframing/prototyping, and/or content optimization and strategy. 2. Must have technical knowledge and proficiency in interaction design technologies (e.g., Figma) and the Adobe Suite, as well as remote collaboration tools. Preferred: 1. Teaching experience at the college level. 2. For candidates with master’s degrees, professional experience in the field of UX. ______________________________________________________________________________________________________ The University of Rhode Island is an equal-opportunity employer. It is the policy of the University of Rhode Island to provide reasonable accommodation when requested by a qualified applicant or employee with a disability. Union Non-Union Faculty Status Academic Year, Part-time End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Professional & Public Writing Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) CV with contact information for three (3) professional references (outside URI ), as one complete document. Posting Information Position Number N/A - Internal Payroll Posting Number F00417 Posting Date 05/22/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/13400 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master's degree in technical communication or related field or a bachelor's degree and three (3) years of professional experience in areas such as UX research, UX analytics, UX writing and/or content design, usability and heuristic evaluation, accessibility, wireframing/prototyping, and/or content optimization and strategy? Yes No * Do you have technical knowledge and proficiency in interaction design technologies (e.g., Figma) and the Adobe Suite, as well as remote collaboration tools? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
