    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16950": {
      "title": "General Manager, Catering and Events",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | General Manager, Catering and Events Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm General Manager, Catering and Events Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02191 Job Title General Manager, Catering and Events Position Number 106841 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 12 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range: $71,000 - $76,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Dining Catering Operations Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by August 31, 2026. Applications received after August 31, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Provide executive leadership and overall management of URI Dining’s Catering and Events business unit, including full-service catering, conferences, commencement activities, donor and VIP events, campus-wide special events, mobile dining operations, and other revenue-generating hospitality services. Responsible for the strategic direction, financial performance, operational effectiveness, customer satisfaction, business development, marketing, staffing, and growth of a comprehensive hospitality operation with total annual revenues exceeding $1.75 million. Develop and implement short- and long-range business plans that support Dining Services strategic priorities while achieving revenue growth, fiscal sustainability, operational excellence, and exceptional guest experiences. Serve as the principal leader for Catering and Events and maintain full accountability for sales performance, budgeting, forecasting, labor management, client relations, operational execution, and service quality. Collaborate closely with the Executive Chef and culinary leadership team to develop innovative menus, enhance guest experiences, and ensure successful execution of all catering and event operations. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Develop and execute annual strategic, operational, marketing, and financial plans for Catering and Events that support departmental goals and long-term growth objectives. Direct all sales, business development, client engagement, and customer relationship activities. Identify opportunities to increase revenue through conferences, donor events, alumni programs, athletic events, summer programs, and other external business opportunities. Establish annual revenue goals, operating budgets, labor targets, customer satisfaction metrics, and performance indicators. Monitor results and implement corrective actions to ensure achievement of established objectives. Maintain full accountability for the financial performance of Catering and Events, including revenue generation, labor management, operating expenses, forecasting, budget preparation, and financial reporting while analyzing revenue trends, labor utilization, food costs, operating expenses, and profitability. Serve as the primary liaison with university departments as the lead client relationship manager. Collaborate with the Executive Chef to develop menus, pricing strategies, service concepts, and special event offerings that meet customer expectations and support financial objectives. Direct all administrative functions associated with Catering and Events, including event scheduling, contract negotiations, customer contracts, billing, invoicing, event documentation, resource allocation, and operational planning. Recruit, train, supervise, mentor, and evaluate staff. Establish and maintain service standards, operating procedures, and performance expectations. Coordinate large-scale University events, commencement activities, conferences, VIP functions, donor events, and special programs requiring extensive logistical planning and cross-functional collaboration. Collaborate with University partners to maximize operational effectiveness and identify new service opportunities. Ensure compliance with all University, State, and Federal regulations relating to food safety, alcohol service, labor standards, transportation, risk management, and event operations. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in hospitality management, Business Administration, Food Service Management, Hotel and Restaurant Management, Event Management, Marketing, or a related field. 2. Minimum of seven years of progressively responsible experience in hospitality, catering, conference services, event management, foodservice operations, or a related field. 3. Minimum of three years of demonstrated management experience with responsibility for budgeting, revenue generation, operational planning, personnel supervision, customer relations, and business development. 4. Strong financial management, along with written and verbal communication skills. 5. Knowledge of food safety principles, HACCP , labor management practices, risk management, contract administration, and regulatory compliance. 6. Ability to work a flexible schedule in support of operational, event, and emergency response requirements. 7. Ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Working knowledge of CBORD Food Service Suite, EMS , CaterTrax, Food Service Suite, point-of-sale systems, or comparable hospitality and foodservice management systems. 2. Experience in higher education dining, conference services, hospitality, hotel operations, contract foodservice, or multi-unit foodservice operations. 3. Demonstrated experience collaborating across departments and building effective partnerships with internal and external stakeholders. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. This position may require frequent evening and weekend work in support of special events, commencement activities, conferences, and catering operations. Posting Date 08/13/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16944 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in hospitality management, Business Administration, Food Service Management, Hotel and Restaurant Management, Event Management, Marketing, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of seven years of progressively responsible experience in hospitality, catering, conference services, event management, foodservice operations, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of three years of demonstrated management experience with responsibility for budgeting, revenue generation, operational planning, personnel supervision, customer relations, and business development? Yes No * Do you have strong financial management, along with written and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have knowledge of food safety principles, HACCP, labor management practices, risk management, contract administration, and regulatory compliance? Yes No * Do you have ability to work a flexible schedule in support of operational, event, and emergency response requirements? Yes No * Do you have ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
