    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16516": {
      "title": "Assistant /Associate Professor in Physical Therapy",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant /Associate Professor in Physical Therapy Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant /Associate Professor in Physical Therapy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 5 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter describing your interest and qualifications for the position. (#2) A complete curriculum vitae including the full contact information for at least three professional references (as one complete document). (#3) A research plan, limited to two pages, describing your current and future research and how it relates to the required qualifications (as one complete document). (#4) A narrative, limited to one page, describing your teaching background and philosophy (as one complete document). (#5) Other Document - reprints of up to 3 publications that you feel best highlight your suitability for the position (as one complete pdf document). Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant /Associate Professor in Physical Therapy Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by May 11, 2026. Applications received after May 11, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ The Department of Physical Therapy at the University of Rhode Island invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor with expertise in research and teaching that aligns with the mission of the Department, College, and University. Negotiated rank is contingent on qualifications and experience. This academic-year appointment begins in August 2026. The Department is part of the College of Health Sciences and is nationally recognized for excellence in teaching, research, service, professional leadership, international opportunities for students, strong clinical partnerships, and an on-site clinic. Each year, the program admits a cohort of 32 students who are taught by a dedicated and experienced faculty. The Physical Therapy Department is located on the Kingston campus in a beautiful rural setting just 15 minutes from ocean and bay beaches. The region offers abundant outdoor recreation opportunities, with the Green and White Mountains only a three-hour drive away. The University of Rhode Island provides a rich array of cultural and intellectual events, including theater, music, athletics, and the Honors Colloquium. Additional cultural and recreational opportunities are easily accessible in Providence (40 minutes), Boston and Cape Cod (90 minutes), and New York City (three hours). KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : The successful candidate will: Demonstrate a strong focus on research productivity and obtaining external funding to support research and graduate students. Develop, lead, and collaborate on research programs leading to peer‑reviewed publications and grant submissions in physical therapy or related fields. Teach graduate-level courses in the Doctor of Physical Therapy ( DPT ) program. Contribute service to the Department, College, University, and/or the profession. Mentor and advise students. Demonstrate experience or potential to engage students in teaching, research, and service. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : Ph.D. (or equivalent) completed by August 2027. Eligibility for physical therapist licensure in Rhode Island. Demonstrated ability to establish an independent research agenda and publish in relevant, peer‑reviewed journals. Demonstrated ability to obtain external funding. Demonstrated teaching ability that complements the existing DPT curriculum. Proficiency in oral communication skills. Proficiency in written communication skills. Current membership in the American Physical Therapy Association ( APTA ). Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. PREFERRED : Demonstrated success in securing external research funding. Demonstrated ability to participate in collaborative research. Interest and/or experience in teaching contemporary professional topics in physical therapy at the graduate level. Experience in mentoring graduate students Evidence of success or strong potential for obtaining external funding to support a productive research program. Relevant clinical experience is desirable. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ This is a 9‑month academic‑year position, beginning five days before the start of the Fall 2026 semester and concluding on Commencement Day the following May. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union AAUP - American Assoc of Univ Professors Status Academic Year, Full-time, Tenure-track, Permanent End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Physical Therapy Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 5 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter describing your interest and qualifications for the position. (#2) A complete curriculum vitae including the full contact information for at least three professional references (as one complete document). (#3) A research plan, limited to two pages, describing your current and future research and how it relates to the required qualifications (as one complete document). (#4) A narrative, limited to one page, describing your teaching background and philosophy (as one complete document). (#5) Other Document – reprints of up to 3 publications that you feel best highlight your suitability for the position (as one complete pdf document). Posting Information Position Number 108567 Posting Number F00518 Posting Date 03/11/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16203 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Research Plan A narrative Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have or will have a Ph.D. (or equivalent) completed by August 2027? Yes No * Do you have eligibility for physical therapist licensure in Rhode Island? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to establish an independent research agenda and publish in relevant, peer reviewed journals? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to obtain external funding? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated teaching ability that complements the existing DPT curriculum? Yes No * Do you have current membership in the American Physical Therapy Association (APTA)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17022": {
      "title": "Catering Coordinator",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Catering Coordinator Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Catering Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02192 Job Title Catering Coordinator Position Number 109348 FTE 1.00 FLSA Non-Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 9 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range:  $55,000 - $60,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Dining Catering Operations Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by August 28, 2026. Applications received after August 28, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Provide administrative, operational, fiscal, and customer service support for URI Dining Catering and Events. Serve as the day-to-day primary coordinator for event administration, client communications, billing, event documentation, scheduling, and logistical support for catering operations. Support the General Manager, Catering and Events, in all unit efforts as needed. Assist with sales activities, event logistics, financial administration, customer service, marketing initiatives, and operational coordination. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Serve as the primary point of contact for routine catering inquiries and event requests. Receive, review, process, and maintain catering orders utilizing designated event management and catering software systems. Assist clients in identifying event needs, menu selections, service requirements, room setups, equipment needs, and logistical details. Prepare event documentation, banquet event orders, invoices, contracts, estimates, and related operational reports. Coordinate communication among clients, culinary staff, operations staff, facilities personnel, vendors, and University departments to ensure successful event execution. Maintain event calendars, staffing schedules, production schedules, delivery schedules, and operational timelines. Assist the General Manager in planning and coordinating conferences, donor events, commencement activities, VIP functions, and special events as needed. Assist with event setup verification, event execution, and post-event follow-up activities. Maintain customer records, sales data, historical event information, and operational files. Process invoices, deposits, billing documents, journal entries, and other financial records while assisting with budget tracking, sales reporting, revenue monitoring, and operational performance reporting. Compile and prepare reports related to sales, customer satisfaction, event activity, labor utilization, and financial performance. Assist with recruiting, onboarding, training, scheduling, and supervising student employees assigned to catering operations. Ensure compliance with University policies, food safety regulations, risk management procedures, and departmental operating standards. Work collaboratively with all University departments to support operational success. Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, catering management software, event management software, point-of-sale systems, CBORD /Food Service Suite, EMS , Microsoft Office applications, financial management systems, database software, and related technology is preferred. Must possess and maintain: • Rhode Island Food Safety Manager Certification • TIPS or equivalent Responsible Alcohol Service Certification • Valid Rhode Island Driver’s License Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in hospitality management, Business Administration, Event Management, Communications, Marketing, Food Service Management, or a related field. 2. Minimum of two years of professional experience in catering, hospitality, conference services, event management, customer service, sales support, foodservice operations, or a related field. 3. Demonstrated experience coordinating events, schedules, logistics, or customer service activities. 4. Demonstrated customer service and communication skills. 5. Must have Rhode Island Food Safety Manager Certification and TIPS Certification or obtain both within six months of appointment. 6. Ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Experience in higher education dining, conference services, hospitality, or event management. 2. Experience with Microsoft Office applications including Word, Excel, Outlook, and PowerPoint. 3. Experience using CBORD Food Service Suite, EMS , CaterTrax, or similar hospitality management systems. 4. Experience with billing, budgeting, accounts receivable, or financial reporting. 5. Experience supervising student employees. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. This position may require frequent evening and weekend work in support of special events, commencement activities, conferences, and catering operations. Posting Date 08/14/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16947 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in hospitality management, Business Administration, Event Management, Communications, Marketing, Food Service Management, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years of professional experience in catering, hospitality, conference services, event management, customer service, sales support, foodservice operations, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience coordinating events, schedules, logistics, or customer service activities? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated customer service and communication skills? Yes No * Do you have Rhode Island Food Safety Manager Certification and TIPS Certification or obtain both within six months of appointment? Yes No * Do you have ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
