    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16540": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I (Infectious Diseases Research Laboratory)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Research Assistant I (Infectious Diseases Research Laboratory) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Research Assistant I (Infectious Diseases Research Laboratory) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 3 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover Letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document - Transcripts (unofficial will be accepted too) Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02097 Job Title Research Assistant I (Infectious Diseases Research Laboratory) Position Number 107661 FTE 1.00 FLSA Non-Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PTAA - Professional/Tech/Admin Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 1 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range:  $35,000 - $45,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department Pharmacy Practice and Clinical Research Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: ( https://jobs.uri.edu ) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded Yes Extension Contingency Notes This is a full time, calendar year position currently funded through 06/26/2027 with anticipated renewal contingent upon continued funding, _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by March 28, 2026. Applications received after March 28, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. _________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Under the supervision of the Principal Investigator(s) or designated laboratory supervisor, the employee shall perform delegated duties in support of infectious diseases research conducted within a Biosafety Level ( BSL -2) laboratory. The employee is required to adhere strictly to all institutional, regulatory, and laboratory policies governing safety, compliance, and research integrity. CONDITION OF EMPLOYMENT : Performance of the essential functions listed above, adherence to all safety and compliance requirements, and maintenance of professional conduct are mandatory conditions of this position. The institution reserves the right to modify duties, restrict laboratory access, or terminate employment in cases of non-compliance, unsafe conduct, or failure to fulfill required responsibilities. KEY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES / FUNCTIONS : The following responsibilities are considered essential functions of this position and are mandatory requirements of employment: Research Support and Technical Duties: Perform laboratory research procedures and experimental protocols as assigned. Assist in the preparation, processing, handling, and analysis of biological specimens and research materials. Accurately record experimental data, observations, and procedures in accordance with laboratory standards and institutional policies. Support ongoing research projects through execution of established methods and protocols. Laboratory Equipment and Instrumentation: Properly operate, maintain, calibrate, and store laboratory instruments and equipment. Immediately report equipment malfunctions, safety concerns, or procedural deviations to the laboratory supervisor. Follow all training requirements prior to operating laboratory equipment. Compliance with Biosafety and Regulatory Requirements: Strictly comply with all biosafety, biosecurity, and institutional safety policies, including BSL -2 containment procedures. Maintain compliance with all applicable federal, state, institutional, and laboratory regulations, including but not limited to OSHA , CDC / NIH biosafety guidelines, and institutional Environmental Health and Safety ( EHS ) policies. Properly use personal protective equipment ( PPE ) and follow required safety protocols at all times. Laboratory Conduct and Professional Responsibilities: Work independently and responsibly under supervisory direction. Maintain laboratory cleanliness, organization, and operational readiness. Protect the integrity, confidentiality, and security of research materials, data, and laboratory resources. Complete all required safety, compliance, and laboratory training prior to performing assigned duties and maintain active certification status as required. Work Schedule and Availability Requirements: The employee is required to maintain a flexible schedule based on experimental needs. This position requires availability outside of standard business hours, including early mornings, evenings, and weekends, for the purpose of time-sensitive sample collection, monitoring experiments, or maintaining research continuity. Physical and Environmental Requirements: The employee must be able to perform the essential functions of this position safely and effectively. These requirements include, but are not limited to: Ability to work safely in a BSL -2 laboratory environment with infectious agents. Ability to stand for extended periods of time. Ability to use hands for fine motor tasks, including pipetting, handling specimens, and operating laboratory equipment. Ability to lift and move laboratory supplies and equipment weighing up to 25 pounds. Ability to wear required personal protective equipment, including gloves, lab coat, eye protection, and respiratory protection if required. Ability to perform repetitive laboratory tasks requiring manual dexterity. Duties and Responsibilities OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties, as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers and printers; word processing, database management, spreadsheet software, laboratory equipment. U.S. Citizenship. Required Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS : 1. Bachelor’s degree in Microbiology, Biology, or related life sciences field. 2. Demonstrated research experience in a higher education setting. 3. Experience with infectious diseases protocols. 4. Demonstrated organizational skills. 5. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 6. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 7. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 8. U.S. Citizenship (to access satellite lab space on Providence Veterans Affairs Campus). _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 03/09/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 3 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover Letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document – Transcripts (unofficial will be accepted too) Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16021 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree in Microbiology, Biology, or related life sciences field? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated research experience in a higher education setting? Yes No * Do you have experience with infectious diseases protocols? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated organizational skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have U.S. Citizenship (in order to access satellite lab space on Providence Veterans Affairs Campus)? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PTAA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
