    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16564": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Research and Scholarship, College of Health Sciences",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Associate Dean for Research and Scholarship, College of Health Sciences Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Associate Dean for Research and Scholarship, College of Health Sciences Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 4 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Research Statement (own research & strategy for building college research (as one complete pdf document). (#4) Diversity Statement Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02132 Job Title Associate Dean for Research and Scholarship, College of Health Sciences Position Number 107125 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 18 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range: $175,000 - $195,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department Dean Health Sciences Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: ( https://jobs.uri.edu ) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Position is full-time calendar year, limited to 06/30/2029 with anticipated renewal. __________________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by April 17, 2026. Applications received after April 17, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. _________________________________________________________________________________________________ The College of Health Sciences includes seven departments (Communicative Disorders, Human Development and Family Science, Kinesiology, Nutrition, Physical Therapy, Psychology, and Public Health), as well as the Interdisciplinary Neuroscience Program, the Osher Lifelong Learning Institute, and the Program in Gerontology. The College offers seven undergraduate degrees with a total enrollment of 2,460 students. The College offers eight master’s degree programs and four doctoral degree programs with a total graduate enrollment of 264 graduate students. There are 90 faculty members in the college. _________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Serve as a member of the College’s Administrative Leadership Team. Help lead the development and direction of the College’s research and scholarship activities. Cultivate externally funded, faculty-led programs of research with an emphasis on NIH , NSF and major foundation funding. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : In collaboration with the Dean and College leadership, provide vision and leadership in planning, goal setting, implementing, and evaluating the College’s research agenda and growth plan. Regularly assess and report on research productivity in the College to help guide strategic planning Assist and advise the Dean, College of Health Sciences, on all matters relating to the College’s research and scholarship. Collaborate with the Chief Business Officer to support the smooth functioning of the pre/post award process. Develop faculty mentoring programs to advance their success in developing and sustaining a fundable research program across the broad range of disciplines in the College of Health Sciences. Mentor PhD students in the development of grant proposals. Serve as a resource for the College in interpreting relevant rules and regulations and liaise with other University entities responsible for research. Facilitate and participate in the development of new and exciting research initiatives/collaborations of relevance to diverse stakeholders from the University, government, and others outside of the University. Coordinate with other Associate Deans for Research and the office of the VP for Research and Economic Development in supporting University-wide research initiatives. Maintain a robust program of externally funded research at the R01 or equivalent level. Engage in teaching as appropriate. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as required and assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers and printers, electronic mail, word processing, database management, spreadsheet software, research statistical and data analysis software as needed. Required Qualifications REQUIRED : 1. PhD or equivalent research-focused degree in a health-related field. 2. Sustained track record of NIH or equivalent funding. 3. Current external research funding. 4. Achievement of teaching, scholarship, and service commensurate with appointment at the rank of Professor eligible for tenure. 5. Sustained publication record. 6. Supervisory experience. 7. Strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 8. Proficiency in written communication skills. 9. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 10. Experience working collaboratively. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO STATEMENT : URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request a reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions Posting Date 03/20/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 4 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Research Statement (own research & strategy for building college research (as one complete pdf document). (#4) Diversity Statement Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16505 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Research Statement Diversity Statement - (justice, equity, diversity and inclusion) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD or equivalent research-focused degree in a health-related field? Yes No * Do you have sustained track record of NIH or equivalent funding? Yes No * Do you have current external research funding? Yes No * Do you have achievement of teaching, scholarship, and service commensurate with appointment at the rank of Professor eligible for tenure? Yes No * Do you have sustained publication record? Yes No * Do you have supervisory experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have experience working collaboratively? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17032": {
      "title": "Landscape Maintenance Technician III",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Landscape Maintenance Technician III Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Landscape Maintenance Technician III Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS: At the time of appointment and continually thereafter as a condition of continued employment: 1. Must possess a valid Commercial Driver’s License (CDL), Class B 2. Must possess a valid Arborist License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management (DEM) 3. Must possess a valid Rhode Island Commercial Pesticide Applicator’s license as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management (DEM) 4. Must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician’s certificate 5. Must possess a Hoisting License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Labor & Training (DLT) Posting Details Position Information Posting Number CS02304 Job Title Landscape Maintenance Technician III Position Number TBD FTE 1.00 FLSA Pay Rate Salary Range $59,684 - $68,574 Pay Grade Level 324A Position Type Classified Civil Service Staff Union C94/L528 - Council 94/Local 528 (Serv/Maint) Status Full-time, Calendar Year, Permanent Restriction or Limitation Reason End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Landscape & Grounds Maintenance Contact(s) Sean Nelson Specialist, Talent Acquisition Office of Human Resource Administration 80 Lower College Road Kingston, RI 02881 Contact Phone/Extension 401-874-5269 Contact Email sean.nelson@uri.edu Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Building(s) Grant Funded Extension Contingent on Funding Date Extension Contingency Notes Duties and Responsibilities ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLES OF WORK PERFORMED : Within the University of Rhode Island ( URI ), to perform and oversee advanced technical and skilled work, including computation of quantities, quality, cost, estimating labor and materials relating to landscape projects at URI and all the properties owned by URI ; to be responsible for and train subordinates on: maintenance of equipment, the application of general use pesticides, professional tree work, planting, watering, sweeping, snow removal, and the utilization of plants used to beautify the university properties; and to do related work as required. To supervise subordinates engaged in cleaning and maintaining parking lots, roadsides, landscape plantings, including transplanting shrubs or trees, pruning trees, tree stump removal, tree stump grinding, weeding, spraying, fertilizing, hydroseeding, rolling and sodding, leaf collection, trimming and mowing grass. To be responsible for the maintenance of shrubbery and other plant materials used to beautify landscape beds, bioretention ponds, swales, slope coverages, parking lots and roadsides. To maintain current knowledge and specific care needs of various plants including trees, shrubs and perennials. To be involved in plant material selection, including plant identification and calculations of quantities for various planting and landscape projects. To supervise maintenance subordinates in special roadside projects such as selective tree and planting projects and appropriate herbicide application procedures dealing with both planted and native flora and fauna. To recommend landscape planting for site improvements and erosion control including grading, filling, sloping, selection of proper plant materials to combat the erosion, seeding and sodding. To perform safety sensitive functions and provide a safe work environment for co-workers and the campus community by following established work and safety rules. As assigned, to operate heavy trucks equipped with plow blades and spreaders to remove snow and ice and spread de-icing materials on sidewalks, parking lots and roadway surfaces. As assigned, to operate mowers or tractors with attached rotary, gang, sickle or other type cutters to control vegetation in ditches, medians and other areas of university owned right-of-way. To operate turf management equipment such as aerator, top-dressing attachment, rototiller, sod cutter, and over seeding equipment. To operate watering equipment such as tow behind water buffalo, water tanks, truck mounted water tanks, hose and reel and other related equipment to maintain healthy plant material on the university campus. Required Qualifications KNOWLEDGE , SKILLS AND CAPACITIES : Advanced knowledge of industry standard landscape maintenance methods, practices and techniques and the ability to apply such methods, practices and techniques, including the safe use of appropriate equipment; advanced knowledge of arboriculture, turf maintenance and safe use of herbicides; knowledge of the methods commonly used in the eradication of insect pests and diseases of ornamental plants; the ability to lay out, coordinate and supervise the work of skilled and unskilled personnel; the ability to direct proper seeding, hydroseeding, sodding and fertilizing methods and practices; the ability to keep records and prepare written reports; the ability to follow oral and written instructions; and related capacities and abilities. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE : Education: Possession of associate degree or higher in Horticulture, Landscape Architecture, Plant Science, Forestry, or another related course study; and Experience: A minimum of seven (7) years of employment in public agency or in private industry involving arboriculture or landscape maintenance at a technical level, including possession of valid Pesticide and Arborist licenses for that duration. Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to environmental conditions. Work Hours 7:30am – 4:00pm – Monday – Friday Saturday and Sunday off Posting Date 09/04/2026 Closing Date 09/14/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS : At the time of appointment and continually thereafter as a condition of continued employment: 1. Must possess a valid Commercial Driver’s License ( CDL ), Class B 2. Must possess a valid Arborist License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management ( DEM ) 3. Must possess a valid Rhode Island Commercial Pesticide Applicator’s license as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management ( DEM ) 4. Must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician’s certificate 5. Must possess a Hoisting License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Labor & Training ( DLT ) Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17031 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Required License Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a state employee who is a member of AFSCME/Council 94? yes no * Do you have advanced knowledge of industry standard landscape maintenance methods, practices and techniques and the ability to apply such methods, practices and techniques, including the safe use of appropriate equipment? (Open Ended Question) * Do you possess a valid Commercial Driver’s License (CDL), Class B? yes no * Do you possess a valid Arborist License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management (DEM) ? yes no * Do you possess a valid Rhode Island Commercial Pesticide Applicator's license as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management (DEM)? yes no * Do you possess a Hoisting License as regulated by the Rhode Island Department of Labor & Training\r\n(DLT)? yes no To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16842": {
      "title": "Marine Research Specialist II",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Marine Research Specialist II Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Marine Research Specialist II Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Name and contact information for 3 professional references. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02177 Job Title Marine Research Specialist II Position Number Job Code # 100708Z FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 7 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range:  $55,000 - $68,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department GSO Research Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: ( https://jobs.uri.edu ) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Narragansett Bay Campus Grant Funded Yes Extension Contingency Notes Position is full-time, calendar year, limited until 9/4/2027 with anticipated renewal. ______________________________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by July 25, 2026. Applications received after (this date) July 25, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Perform experimental and developmental work in support of major research programs. Responsible for the planning, operation, and management of significant experimental/research programs. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Use established analytical, experimental and investigative methods and techniques, using either gas or liquid chromatography and mass spectrometry, with minor modifications and adaptations. Collect, process, monitor and analyze samples and/or data linked to trace organic compounds in water, sediment/soil, biota and air. Maintain laboratory and research instruments for conformance with research priorities and safety concerns. Responsible for maintenance of good laboratory practices and safety. Prepare and publish manuscripts containing results of research efforts. Develop experimental procedures and techniques for resolution of unique scientific/research problems in the field of pollutant sampling and detection in the field. Assist in supervisory and administrative duties related to research programs. Provide guidance and assistance to graduate students and supervise undergraduate research assistants. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Assist in fieldwork for projects within lab with focuses other than pollutant sampling. Perform additional duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Equipment: Gas or liquid chromatography; mass spectrometer; GC- ECD , GC-MS, GC-MS/MS. GC-Q-ToF; HPLC -MS/MS, UPLC -Q-ToF; Personal computers, printers, external hard drives. Software: Word processing, database management, spreadsheet, instrument operating software. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in Chemical Oceanography, Chemistry or related field. 2. Minimum two years of relevant research support experience (i.e., field sampling; laboratory support; chemical analysis). 3. Demonstrated experience in an area of specialization (i.e., environmental trace organic sample analysis). 4. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 5. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 6. Demonstrated organizational skills. 7. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 8. Must be able to work at sea, as needed. 9.. Must have a valid driver’s license. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Demonstrated experience in field-based sampling platforms; and demonstrated experience in LC-MS/MS or GC-MS instrument operation and maintenance. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 07/10/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Name and contact information for 3 professional references. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16816 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree in Chemical Oceanography, Chemistry or related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum two years of relevant research support experience (i.e., field sampling; laboratory support; chemical analysis)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in an area of specialization (i.e., environmental trace organic sample analysis)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated organizational skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Are you able to work at sea, as needed? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver’s license? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16988": {
      "title": "Senior Integration Programmer",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Senior Integration Programmer Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Senior Integration Programmer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02196 Job Title Senior Integration Programmer Position Number 106618 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PTAA - Professional/Tech/Admin Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 12 Pay Grade Range Hiring Salary Range:  $70,000 - $80,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Info Tech Services Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by September 11, 2026. Applications received after September 11, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE POSITION IS IMMEDIATELY ELIGIBLE FOR A FULLY REMOTE WORK SCHEDULE . POSITION SUMMARY : The Senior Integration Programmer is a technical resource responsible for the design, development, configuration, and maintenance of enterprise application integrations and data flows across a wide range of enterprise applications—including ERP (PeopleSoft, Workday), procurement (Jaggaer), CRM (Slate, Salesforce), and student success applications. This role focuses on hands-on implementation of integration platforms, data synchronization, and middleware solutions that enable seamless communication between core technology platforms serving all business and academic units at the University of Rhode Island. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Analyze, configure, develop, test, implement, and maintain enterprise applications and integration solutions, including but not limited to PeopleSoft, Workday, Jaggaer, Slate, Salesforce, and student success platforms. Develop technical specifications and system procedures to support university-wide administrative, academic, and student success processes. Implement new modules, features, integrations, and enhancements as required by university business and academic units. Troubleshoot, diagnose, and resolve complex system issues in collaboration with IT staff and functional users. Maintain and update application documentation, technical procedures, and project plans according to departmental standards. Review technical deliverables and code to ensure quality, security, and compliance with university and industry standards. Coordinate and schedule technical work, manage assigned projects, and ensure timely delivery of solutions. Assist in evaluating and deploying vendor updates, patches, and application upgrades. Provide technical support and guidance to application users and internal IT staff. Remain current with evolving technologies and best practices relevant to enterprise, ERP , procurement, CRM , and student success applications. Design, develop, test, implement, and maintain enterprise application integrations using Informatica IICS and other iPaaS platforms. Develop and maintain data mapping specifications, integration workflows, and ETL processes. Configure and manage integration middleware platforms including Informatica IICS , Apache Airflow, and related tools. Manage integration deployment pipelines and version control across development, test, and production environments. Monitor integration performance, troubleshoot data flow issues, and optimize integration solutions. Collaborate with business analysts and application teams to gather integration requirements and translate them into technical specifications. Other Duties and Responsibilities: The position may require after-hours or on-call work to support system maintenance and issue resolution. Perform additional duties as needed. Licenses, Tools, and Equipment: Proficiency with Informatica IICS , Apache Airflow, version control systems (Git/GitHub), API development and testing tools, Linux/Unix command-line interfaces, and database query and optimization tools. Required Qualifications Qualifications Required: 1. Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or related field. 2. Minimum of 1-2 years of hands-on experience with Informatica IICS or similar enterprise integration platforms in production environments. 3. Demonstrated hands-on experience with Informatica IICS (Intelligent Cloud Services) including cloud data integration, mappings, and task scheduling. 4. Demonstrated experience with ETL / ELT tools and data integration platforms. 5. Demonstrated experience with Linux and Windows Server operating systems. 6. Demonstrated experience with relational databases and SQL optimization for integration scenarios. 7. Demonstrated experience with integration-focused programming languages/tools such as SQL , Python, Java, and scripting languages. 8. Demonstrated ability to independently manage application configurations, technical projects, and troubleshooting. 9. Demonstrated ability to develop technical documentation and procedures. 10. Demonstrated strong analytical and problem-solving skills. 11. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple assignments and priorities. 12. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 13. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 14. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications Preferred: 1. Demonstrated hands-on experience with Apache Airflow for workflow orchestration and data pipeline management. 2. Demonstrated experience with PeopleSoft integration and customization, particularly in HR, Finance, or Campus Solutions modules. 3. Demonstrated experience with Workday integrations. 4. Demonstrated experience with Oracle databases, including database administration and performance tuning for integration workloads. 5. Demonstrated experience with Linux and Windows Server system administration and scripting. 6. Demonstrated experience with RESTful APIs, web services, and cloud integration platforms. 7. Demonstrated experience integrating third-party SaaS solutions with ERP , CRM , student success, or other enterprise systems. 8. Demonstrated experience with CI/CD practices and integration deployment automation. 9. Demonstrated experience with data governance and master data management. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions Environmental Conditions: This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 08/26/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16963 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of 1-2 years of hands-on experience with Informatica IICS or similar enterprise integration platforms in production environments? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated hands-on experience with Informatica IICS (Intelligent Cloud Services) including cloud data integration, mappings, and task scheduling? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with ETL/ELT tools and data integration platforms? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with Linux and Windows Server operating systems? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with relational databases and SQL optimization for integration scenarios? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with integration-focused programming languages/tools such as SQL, Python, Java, and scripting languages? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to independently manage application configurations, technical projects, and troubleshooting? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to develop technical documentation and procedures? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong analytical and problem-solving skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to manage multiple assignments and priorities? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PTAA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
